# Gate EVERY HTTP request to this stack behind HTTP Basic auth — the page, the
# /screen WebSocket upgrade, /setup, /take, /release, /pony/act, /logs. Without
# this, anyone with the URL can bind the VNC display and drive the pony's Chrome,
# including whatever it is logged into. (Health checks on /healthz stay open.)
#
# The password is a TENANT SECRET. Set it, and the gate closes:
#   txco auth tenant secrets set EXAMPLE_BROWSER_PW --tenant <this stack's tenant>
# then reach the stack as user `human`, password = that secret. The browser
# prompts once and reuses the credentials for the /screen WebSocket and the
# fetch() calls, so one prompt protects the whole flow.
#
# secrets.password.optional=true lets the op RUN when the secret is unset (so it
# can emit a verdict and issue a 401 prompt rather than being skipped);
# allow_unconfigured=false is the DECISION, visible here: this stack hands over a
# logged-in browser, so it FAILS CLOSED — no EXAMPLE_BROWSER_PW set ⇒ nobody gets
# in (401 everywhere until you set one). The secret never reaches the envelope:
# the op consumes it and emits only a verdict (@computed.basic_auth_ok),
# compared constant-time.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path != "/healthz"
  WITH user = "human",
       secrets.password.secret = "EXAMPLE_BROWSER_PW",
       secrets.password.optional = true,
       allow_unconfigured = false
  EXEC "txco://basic-auth-verify"
